# f4 = run, f5 = each
# An instance of Heir is the prototype of Third and holds a method under the name of a method of Heir: one object of Heir hides it, and the guard that speaks of every object of Heir ends when that
# method is laid. The text says so: an instance of Heir is stored under `prototype`. So run() asks of Heir the guard that speaks of what stands above the objects, which a hiding object does not end;
# the object that it made itself has nothing beside its fields.
# RUN(GUARD): walk f4 mechanisms=all
# GUARD: kind=MemberUnchangedAbove layout=L1 key="area"
# each() looks at the objects that it finds in the list: any of them may be the one that hides the method.
# RUN(LOOK): walk f5 mechanisms=all
# LOOK: HasNoExtraProperties
